into thinking you killed yourself?

388
00:41:41,373 --> 00:41:43,334
Look at this cheeky little bastard.

389
00:41:46,170 --> 00:41:51,050
You got work done like this
just to steal his identity?

390
00:41:57,139 --> 00:41:58,349
Did you send the tip?

391
00:42:04,480 --> 00:42:07,900
This fucking bastard. I like your honesty.

392
00:42:08,484 --> 00:42:12,238
Myeong-su said if we went after Noja,
everyone would get dragged in.

393
00:42:12,321 --> 00:42:13,656
Myeong-su said that?

394
00:42:14,406 --> 00:42:16,742
- Why would he?
- Well, money. What else?

395
00:42:17,910 --> 00:42:18,744
Money?

396
00:42:20,496 --> 00:42:22,289
Fuck, my missing money?

397
00:42:24,416 --> 00:42:25,668
That's right.

398
00:42:25,751 --> 00:42:26,585
That money

399
00:42:27,086 --> 00:42:28,504
is with me.

400
00:42:28,587 --> 00:42:31,799
Myeong-su said he was just the front,
so he'd be out in no time.

401
00:42:31,882 --> 00:42:34,927
He told me to keep it
and go halves when he gets out.

402
00:42:40,641 --> 00:42:43,561
What do you think?
Should we go into business together?

403
00:42:44,853 --> 00:42:47,648
- What?
- I mean, I have the money.

404
00:42:47,731 --> 00:42:50,234
And if I get caught,
you'll get caught too.

405
00:42:50,734 --> 00:42:51,569
Why would I?

406
00:42:52,152 --> 00:42:54,029
Well, because I'm gonna snitch on you.

407
00:42:54,113 --> 00:42:57,825
You remember my girlfriend
who turned up in the Hangang River, right?

408
00:43:25,394 --> 00:43:27,521
What are you talking about,
you fucking bastard?

409
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:29,773
It was your identity I bought back then.

410
00:43:29,857 --> 00:43:31,609
Oh boy, I forgot to tell you.

411
00:43:31,692 --> 00:43:32,776
Damn it.

412
00:43:33,402 --> 00:43:37,615
I sold my girlfriend's identity
to you recently.

413
00:43:37,698 --> 00:43:39,950
I put the documents together
and sent them to you.

414
00:43:41,035 --> 00:43:42,202
Don't you remember?

415
00:43:42,703 --> 00:43:44,204
"So Min-yeong."

416
00:43:44,705 --> 00:43:46,582
Do these belong to the one in the morgue?

417
00:43:46,665 --> 00:43:47,708
Yes.

418
00:43:47,791 --> 00:43:48,959
The Hangang River?

419
00:43:49,043 --> 00:43:50,586
She was your girlfriend?

420
00:43:51,086 --> 00:43:54,715
The cops got a fucking tip
saying it was murder, and…

421
00:44:00,512 --> 00:44:01,347
Did you kill her?

422
00:44:07,227 --> 00:44:08,646
Well, Mr. Park.

423
00:44:10,189 --> 00:44:11,523
See,

424
00:44:11,607 --> 00:44:15,736
the important thing is she turned up dead
in the Hangang River,

425
00:44:16,236 --> 00:44:19,323
and you sold her identity to someone.

426
00:44:19,406 --> 00:44:22,660
It doesn't matter
whether you killed her or I did.

427
00:44:22,743 --> 00:44:25,496
What I'm saying is,
we're in the same boat.

428
00:44:28,832 --> 00:44:29,667
I mean…

429
00:44:30,876 --> 00:44:33,545
You are the one who inspired me.

430
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:37,174
Identity fraud. That's a great skill.

431
00:44:37,257 --> 00:44:40,094
Well, that skill got you
tangled up in all this.

432
00:44:40,177 --> 00:44:41,387
It's a long story.

433
00:44:41,470 --> 00:44:42,805
It won't end today.

434
00:44:43,514 --> 00:44:45,391
Anyway, are we working together or what?

435
00:44:45,474 --> 00:44:48,018
You bastard. What the hell is your deal?

436
00:44:53,065 --> 00:44:54,983
You goddamn monster.

437
00:44:55,526 --> 00:44:57,403
You're not even human.

438
00:44:58,946 --> 00:45:00,572
You fucking bastard.

439
00:45:01,198 --> 00:45:03,617
Hey.

440
00:45:05,411 --> 00:45:06,495
Today,

441
00:45:06,578 --> 00:45:09,707
I'll dig your grave here,
you fucking bastard.

442
00:45:09,790 --> 00:45:11,333
What about your money?

443
00:45:12,376 --> 00:45:14,962
I don't need that money,
you fucking bastard.

444
00:45:15,045 --> 00:45:16,130
This time,

445
00:45:17,214 --> 00:45:18,799
you die for real.

446
00:45:22,553 --> 00:45:23,637
That's fine too.

447
00:45:38,277 --> 00:45:39,445
But

448
00:45:39,945 --> 00:45:43,031
the investigation's not gonna stop
just because I'm gone.

449
00:45:43,115 --> 00:45:45,951
You have a cop on your tail, right?
I set that up too.

450
00:45:46,034 --> 00:45:50,372
And Major Crimes is all over this too.
This isn't gonna end that easily.

451
00:45:50,456 --> 00:45:52,750
I never meant to meet you either.

452
00:45:52,833 --> 00:45:55,335
But what can I do? Things got messed up.

453
00:45:55,836 --> 00:45:58,464
Let's make it through together. Okay?

454
00:45:58,547 --> 00:46:00,716
Please just do as I say.

455
00:46:01,300 --> 00:46:02,301
But

456
00:46:02,801 --> 00:46:03,719
you need to hurry.

457
00:46:04,219 --> 00:46:06,597
Or we'll both have to delete
our characters.

458
00:46:10,601 --> 00:46:11,477
You

459
00:46:13,020 --> 00:46:14,897
even had your face completely redone.

460
00:46:16,648 --> 00:46:18,150
Why are you doing this?

461
00:46:28,160 --> 00:46:29,411
This bastard…

462
00:46:29,912 --> 00:46:31,038
You know?

463
00:46:31,121 --> 00:46:32,915
The bastard who looks like this

464
00:46:33,624 --> 00:46:35,459
took everything from me.

465
00:46:35,959 --> 00:46:37,878
I have to take it back.

466
00:46:46,136 --> 00:46:48,430
If he wins, you're fucked.

467
00:46:49,056 --> 00:46:51,225
Like it or not, we're in the same boat.

468
00:46:51,725 --> 00:46:52,851
And…

469
00:46:52,935 --> 00:46:55,145
Why does it matter who I am?

470
00:46:55,771 --> 00:46:57,439
Just think about your money.

471
00:47:00,651 --> 00:47:02,611
Find the uncle and get rid of him!

472
00:47:03,111 --> 00:47:04,238
I'm counting on you!

473
00:47:19,336 --> 00:47:22,047
This is his uncle's house?

474
00:47:29,388 --> 00:47:30,806
Why are you taking it out on…

475
00:47:31,598 --> 00:47:34,685
If your partner's a dumbass,
at least you should be smart, you idiot!

476
00:47:34,768 --> 00:47:36,144
Come on, sir.

477
00:47:36,228 --> 00:47:38,021
It's not his fault.

478
00:47:39,273 --> 00:47:40,482
You little…

479
00:47:41,149 --> 00:47:44,319
Fuck, are we on vacation or something?
Everyone's so cheerful.

480
00:47:44,403 --> 00:47:45,737
Hey, you bastard, you…

481
00:47:46,321 --> 00:47:49,408
Fine! I'll submit a written apology, okay?

482
00:47:49,992 --> 00:47:52,244
The window frames are covered in dust.

483
00:47:52,327 --> 00:47:54,538
- He must've been away for a long time.
- What?

484
00:47:54,621 --> 00:47:56,415
I'll go ask the next-door neighbor.

485
00:47:57,624 --> 00:47:58,834
Please.

486
00:47:59,585 --> 00:48:01,295
Pretty fucking please,

487
00:48:02,421 --> 00:48:05,340
act like a cop and behave, okay?

488
00:48:10,012 --> 00:48:14,975
Out of all 128,636 cops in Korea,
he's the bastard least like a cop.

489
00:48:19,813 --> 00:48:22,566
Oh, Han? He's not here.

490
00:48:22,649 --> 00:48:24,818
He went to a nursing home
a few months ago.

491
00:48:25,903 --> 00:48:26,987
A nursing home?

492
00:48:28,113 --> 00:48:32,242
He did <i>meoguri </i>for a long time.
I guess it wasn't good for his health.

493
00:48:32,326 --> 00:48:34,411
<i>Meoguri</i>? What's <i>meoguri</i>?

494
00:48:34,494 --> 00:48:35,329
Did he get hurt?

495
00:48:35,412 --> 00:48:36,830
No, he didn't get hurt.

496
00:48:37,331 --> 00:48:40,667
He can't control his own body properly,
even though he's still young.

497
00:48:42,169 --> 00:48:45,339
But someone else
came looking for him earlier too.

498
00:48:45,923 --> 00:48:47,507
- Who?
- He said he was his nephew.

499
00:48:48,675 --> 00:48:50,802
I didn't know he had family.

500
00:48:51,303 --> 00:48:52,888
He lived alone the whole time.

501
00:48:54,222 --> 00:48:55,432
Which nursing home is it?

502
00:48:57,142 --> 00:48:58,435
He has Alzheimer's.

503
00:48:58,936 --> 00:49:01,605
He's always like that,
so he probably won't recognize you.

504
00:49:02,356 --> 00:49:04,316
We thought he was alone.

505
00:49:04,816 --> 00:49:06,610
Should I register him as your dependent?

506
00:49:07,235 --> 00:49:08,570
A dependent?

507
00:49:12,866 --> 00:49:15,243
I can't even support myself.

508
00:49:23,210 --> 00:49:24,711
Why didn't you come look for me?

509
00:49:30,217 --> 00:49:31,176
Tell me.

510
00:49:32,719 --> 00:49:33,553
Huh?

511
00:49:34,096 --> 00:49:35,806
Tell me.

512
00:49:36,306 --> 00:49:38,141
You even came to the funeral.

513
00:49:38,725 --> 00:49:41,311
- Sir.
- If we had someone…

514
00:49:41,395 --> 00:49:44,231
If we had even just one person,
we wouldn't be like this.

515
00:49:44,314 --> 00:49:45,816
Both of us!

516
00:49:49,486 --> 00:49:50,696
Fuck.

517
00:49:54,658 --> 00:49:55,492
Are you okay?

518
00:51:04,186 --> 00:51:05,812
I'm Je Moon-jae.

519
00:51:07,314 --> 00:51:08,356
I'm Je Moon-jae.

520
00:51:10,567 --> 00:51:11,818
I'm Je Moon-jae!

521
00:51:12,736 --> 00:51:13,570
No.

522
00:51:14,071 --> 00:51:15,072
No!

523
00:51:16,156 --> 00:51:17,240
DEOKAM NURSING HOME

524
00:51:18,909 --> 00:51:20,243
Then who am I?

525
00:52:30,730 --> 00:52:31,773
Bastard!

526
00:52:32,899 --> 00:52:34,734
Fucking bastard. Seriously.

527
00:52:36,069 --> 00:52:37,571
Put that down and fight me.

528
00:52:37,654 --> 00:52:40,031
There are no bullets left in that,
you dumbass.

529
00:52:41,241 --> 00:52:44,536
One blank, three live rounds,
and one empty chamber!

530
00:52:45,203 --> 00:52:47,539
What took you so long,
you fucking bastard?

531
00:52:47,622 --> 00:52:49,833
I've been waiting in this town for ages!

532
00:52:56,464 --> 00:52:57,883
Did you

533
00:52:58,633 --> 00:53:00,260
kill my buddy?

534
00:53:03,847 --> 00:53:04,848
This is…

535
00:53:07,350 --> 00:53:08,977
where you die.

536
00:53:09,477 --> 00:53:10,520
And

537
00:53:11,688 --> 00:53:13,773
it won't be painless. Got it?

538
00:53:14,774 --> 00:53:15,984
Fucking bastard.

539
00:53:18,695 --> 00:53:20,906
You fucking bastard.

540
00:53:46,765 --> 00:53:48,475
Fuck.

541
00:53:50,769 --> 00:53:51,895
I guess

542
00:53:53,230 --> 00:53:54,231
this is where I die.

543
00:54:02,113 --> 00:54:03,448
- Check the CCTV.
- Okay.

544
00:54:03,531 --> 00:54:05,575
- Don't push yourself too hard.
- Okay.

545
00:54:07,160 --> 00:54:08,662
Hello. Mr. Han Hui-su…

546
00:54:09,162 --> 00:54:10,580
Where's Mr. Han Hui-su?

547
00:54:10,664 --> 00:54:12,415
What's this about?

548
00:54:12,916 --> 00:54:14,209
We're with the police.

549
00:54:14,876 --> 00:54:16,586
Where's Mr. Han Hui-su?

550
00:54:17,420 --> 00:54:21,508
When I told him he had Alzheimer's,
he cursed and stormed out.

551
00:54:22,175 --> 00:54:23,593
How long ago was that?

552
00:54:23,677 --> 00:54:25,095
About an hour ago.

553
00:54:37,857 --> 00:54:38,692
Hey.

554
00:54:39,609 --> 00:54:42,404
Maybe he just left
after finding out about his condition.

555
00:54:45,490 --> 00:54:46,950
What can he prove?

556
00:54:47,033 --> 00:54:48,493
He can't even recognize himself.

557
00:54:49,160 --> 00:54:50,161
I know.

558
00:54:50,662 --> 00:54:53,665
He's the only one who can recognize
who the real Je Moon-jae is.

559
00:54:58,044 --> 00:55:00,046
- Let's go.
- Damn it.

560
00:55:12,100 --> 00:55:13,226
Moon-jae.

561
00:55:19,774 --> 00:55:21,109
Moon-jae.

562
00:55:26,239 --> 00:55:27,365
Moon-jae.

563
00:55:40,253 --> 00:55:41,588
I've been

564
00:55:42,714 --> 00:55:44,007
looking for you everywhere.

565
00:55:49,304 --> 00:55:50,847
Moon-jae!

566
00:55:50,930 --> 00:55:52,474
<i>Moon-jae, where are you?</i>

567
00:55:59,898 --> 00:56:01,358
Moon-jae!

568
00:56:02,734 --> 00:56:04,110
Moon-jae!

569
00:56:05,487 --> 00:56:07,072
Moon-jae, where are you?

570
00:56:07,155 --> 00:56:07,989
Moon-jae…

571
00:56:11,993 --> 00:56:13,370
<i>Why are you here?</i>

572
00:56:15,580 --> 00:56:17,540
<i>I've been looking for you everywhere.</i>

573
00:56:20,794 --> 00:56:24,297
I've been looking for you everywhere.

574
